			"Message": "docs(Rest): Annotate entry points, config structs, and compiler options with rustdoc\n\nAdd module-level (`//!`) and item-level (`///`) documentation comments across Source/Binary.rs, Source/Library.rs, Source/Main.rs, Source/Struct/Binary/mod.rs, Source/Struct/SWC.rs, and Source/Struct/mod.rs.\n\nModule-level doc comments describe the purpose of each file or sub-module. Item-level comments annotate all public struct fields (CompilerConfig, Option, CompilerMetrics, FileInfo), enum variants (ModuleFormat), and methods (from_str, as_str) with brief descriptions of their role in the Rest compilation pipeline. The Library.rs module page gains an Architecture section linking to the project's architectural overview.\n\nNo runtime behavior is affected. All pre-existing module declarations and re-exports are preserved.",
